# Internal checkout (Cursor agents)

External releases strip `.github/` and `not_shipped/`. If those paths are missing, follow root
[AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) only — do not error on missing internal paths.

When `not_shipped/docs/` exists (normal internal clone):

1. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first (shipped tree: designs, builds, safe edits).
2. Read [not_shipped/docs/GETTING_STARTED.md](not_shipped/docs/GETTING_STARTED.md) — pick the active
   project under `not_shipped/docs/projects/<slug>/`.
3. Read that project's `AGENTS.md` (rules) and `TODO.md` (living plan) before editing.

Horizontal reference: [not_shipped/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md](not_shipped/docs/DEVELOPMENT.md) (Makefile,
regtest, formatting). Customer README policy:
[not_shipped/docs/guides/USER_FACING_README.md](not_shipped/docs/guides/USER_FACING_README.md).

## Quartus / ARC (Intel dev hosts)

Quartus is not on `PATH` until ARC loads tools. Wrap Quartus-dependent commands:

```bash
arc shell --no-inherit $(cat .github/arc_resource.txt) -- $COMMAND
```

Use for `quartus_sh`, hardware `make` targets, `make -j style-check-readme-metadata`, and similar.
After any shipped README edit, verify with
`arc shell --no-inherit $(cat .github/arc_resource.txt) -- make -j style-check-readme-metadata`.
Details: [not_shipped/docs/AGENTS.md](not_shipped/docs/AGENTS.md).

## CI / workflow work only

Workflow YAML and migration plan stay beside workflows — start at
[.github/workflows/README.md](.github/workflows/README.md) and
[.github/workflows/WORKFLOW_DEVELOPMENT.md](.github/workflows/WORKFLOW_DEVELOPMENT.md).
Project rules: [not_shipped/docs/projects/artifact-migration/AGENTS.md](not_shipped/docs/projects/artifact-migration/AGENTS.md).
